  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Use the quadratic formula to find the zeroes $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ of each quadratic function. Hence write the function in factored form, $f(x)=a(x-\\alpha)(x-\\beta)$, where $a$ is its leading coefficient.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p38-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2-6x+4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes $3\\pm\\sqrt5$.\n\n$f(x)=(x-3-\\sqrt5)(x-3+\\sqrt5)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-6)^2-4(1)(4)=20\\\\x&=\\frac{6\\pm\\sqrt{20}}2\\\\x&=3\\pm\\sqrt5\\\\f(x)&=(x-3-\\sqrt5)(x-3+\\sqrt5)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2+2x-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes $-1\\pm\\sqrt2$.\n\n$f(x)=(x+1-\\sqrt2)(x+1+\\sqrt2)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=2^2-4(1)(-1)=8\\\\x&=\\frac{-2\\pm\\sqrt8}2\\\\x&=-1\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\f(x)&=(x+1-\\sqrt2)(x+1+\\sqrt2)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2-3x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes $\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt5}2$.\n\n$f(x)=\\left(x-\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt5}2\\right)\\left(x-\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt5}2\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-3)^2-4(1)(1)=5\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt5}2\\\\f(x)&=\\left(x-\\frac{3+\\sqrt5}2\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{3-\\sqrt5}2\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=3x^2+6x+2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes $\\dfrac{-3\\pm\\sqrt3}3$.\n\n$f(x)=3\\left(x+\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt3}3\\right)\\left(x+\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt3}3\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=6^2-4(3)(2)=12\\\\x&=\\frac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{12}}6\\\\x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt3}3\\\\f(x)&=3\\left(x+\\frac{3-\\sqrt3}3\\right)\\left(x+\\frac{3+\\sqrt3}3\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor $3$ preserves the leading coefficient.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=-x^2+3x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes $\\dfrac{3\\pm\\sqrt{13}}2$.\n\n$f(x)=-\\left(x-\\dfrac{3+\\sqrt{13}}2\\right)\\left(x-\\dfrac{3-\\sqrt{13}}2\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=3^2-4(-1)(1)=13\\\\x&=\\frac{-3\\pm\\sqrt{13}}{-2}\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pm\\sqrt{13}}2\\\\f(x)&=-\\left(x-\\frac{3+\\sqrt{13}}2\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{3-\\sqrt{13}}2\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor $-1$ preserves the leading coefficient.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p38-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=-2x^2-x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Zeroes $-1,\\tfrac12$.\n\n$f(x)=-2(x+1)(x-\\tfrac12)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-1)^2-4(-2)(1)=9\\\\x&=\\frac{1\\pm\\sqrt9}{-4}\\\\x&=-1\\text{ or }\\frac12\\\\f(x)&=-2(x+1)\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nThe factor $-2$ preserves the leading coefficient.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
  },
